# Issue #1087: a network change while media flows. Each end has two interfaces (ICE pairs on both, the best one
# selected); at 10 s the sender's selected interface stops passing traffic (a firewall rule on its address, as
# libwebrtc's ICE failover tests do), and ICE moves the call to the other interface without an ICE restart.
name ice_network_change
describe The sender's interface fails at 10 s on clean_link's link; ICE recovers on its other interface (transport ice, #1087)
transport ice
compare off
ice_fail a 10s
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=25ms queue=300ms
expect setup.connected == 1
# Measured on seeds 1-5: one audio interruption of 3552-3563 ms (ICE's 2.5 s receiving timeout, then the switch to
# the pair on the other interface), one video freeze of 4098-4170 ms, render 25.6-25.7 fps, no send failures.
# libwebrtc's side of this scenario isn't measured (sm_compare runs direct calls); its receiving timeout is the same
# 2.5 s (IceConfig::receiving_timeout, p2p_transport_channel.cc).
expect transport.send_failures == 0
expect transport.local_candidate_type == 0
expect audio.interruptions <= 1
expect audio.longest_interruption_ms < 4000
expect video.longest_freeze_ms < 4500
expect video.render_fps >= 25
